00:43:52,078 --> 00:44:12,192
My colleagues, I was not involved in this part of the project, but they basically build a graph where they keep track of the amount of crosstalk between actors and migrate the actors in order to get the chatty ones co-located on the same server.

388
00:44:12,432 --> 00:44:16,912
Um that appeared in Eurosys a few years ago.

389
00:44:19,022 --> 00:44:25,392
it's not widely used, it comes up, but it doesn't seem to be a real pain.

