00:55:49,632 --> 00:56:00,772
They didn't like the fact that there were all these transaction manager services around because that meant they had to deploy them in a separate cluster and and keep track of all of that.

504
00:56:01,232 --> 00:56:07,152
Um it was just um it was just too too complicated for what they wanted.

505
00:56:07,392 --> 00:56:14,992
Um, and moreover, they thought that trans centralized transaction manager, even though we we knew it was very high performance, we've carefully optimized it.

506
00:56:15,152 --> 00:56:18,432
They said, gee, you know, we don't like centralized anything in this system.

507
00:56:18,592 --> 00:56:21,860
It looks like it's going to be too costly, it's going to be a bottleneck.

508
00:56:22,382 --> 00:56:25,220
And so we had to go back and redo the whole thing.

509
00:56:25,792 --> 00:56:33,632
Um and and so we came up with um single object transactions, we're able to resolve their dependencies locally.

510
00:56:33,872 --> 00:56:41,472
Um, we have we we had a transaction manager embedded in each object so there were no separate transaction managers.

511
00:56:41,792 --> 00:56:48,352
Um, and because the objects were geo-distributed, you got geo-distributed transactions out of this, so everybody was happy.

